      "content": "When encountering a \"VPN Connection Timeout,\" please follow this comprehensive diagnostic procedure to isolate and resolve the network connectivity interruption that is preventing a secure tunnel establishment. Initially, conduct a fundamental check of your local network infrastructure by verifying that your computer has a stable, active internet connection through a regular web browser, ensuring the issue is specific to the VPN service. Proceed to perform a complete system reboot, which involves shutting down your computer entirely, waiting one full minute, and then restarting it to refresh all local network drivers and processes. If the timeouts continue following the restart, carefully examine the VPN client software for any pending updates or known compatibility issues with your current operating system version and apply any available patches immediately. Furthermore, temporarily disable any overly aggressive third-party firewalls or antivirus suites to rule out interference from local security programs actively blocking the VPN handshake packets. Finally, if all local troubleshooting steps fail, the connection issue likely resides on the server side, warranting immediate escalation to the OmniCorp IT Support Desk with detailed notes from this diagnostic process.",
