      "content": "Understanding the core function of a Virtual Private Network (VPN) is crucial before troubleshooting connection timeouts; essentially, a VPN creates an encrypted, secure tunnel over a public network, safeguarding your data as you access OmniCorp resources remotely. Timeouts generally occur because the client either cannot establish that initial secure handshake with the server, or the established connection is being prematurely dropped due to network instability somewhere along the path. To begin resolving this, ensure your foundational internet access is rock solid by testing multiple websites, confirming the timeout is not simply a general ISP issue. Next, systematically address local machine integrity: fully terminate all background applications that consume significant bandwidth, such as cloud synchronization tools or large download managers, and execute a full system restart to clear any transient memory errors or hung network resources.\n\nIn deep-dive diagnostics, you must consider security software interference; sophisticated firewalls and security suites often incorrectly flag legitimate VPN traffic as a security threat, necessitating a temporary, controlled test where these specific programs are disabled. If this does not resolve the connectivity problem, the focus shifts to network hardware by power cycling both your local modem and router sequentially, allowing a full minute between each power cycle to ensure a complete hardware reset. Furthermore, if you are using a client application, verifying",
